    "reason": "await reads as an identifier, as tree-sitter-javascript 0.25 makes it. Outside async code that is correct TypeScript: function f(await) {}, var v = { [await]: x }. Inside async functions, async generators, class static blocks and module top level, tsc reads await as an operator and rejects it without an operand (TS1109) or as a generic call (await <T>(1)). A context-free grammar cannot tell those contexts apart without duplicating every expression rule for async code, so the grammar accepts this invalid code. Example pair: asyncFunctionDeclaration8_es2017.ts (valid, parses) and asyncFunctionDeclaration9_es2017.ts (the same line inside an async function, invalid, also parses).",
